you bring up great points related to former president trump’s success in driving economic expansion through tax reduction, deregulation and infrastructure investment. There are certainly noticeable improvements witnessed in specific sectors however; when evaluating overall impact particularly pertaining social welfare, I have trouble determining how these factors adequately addressed systemic inequalities which hindered meaningful advancement of previously marginalized groups. Do you believe his policy framework effectively bridged America’s socioeconomic divide in areas like racial equity, women

